course: dictionary
lesson: 4584
title: Helplessly: no power in the moment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Helplessly comes from helpless, which means having no power to help yourself. The ending -less means without, and -ly turns the word into an adverb, so it tells us how something happens.
explain: Read the clues in context: «poor Mole at last gave up the struggle, and cried freely and helplessly and openly». Mole has tried to stop crying and cannot. Gave up the struggle tells you he could no longer fight it, so helplessly means he could not stop himself.
explain: The word can also mean unable to stop, as in «laughed helplessly». Ask yourself: is the person stuck, unable to change what is happening? If so, helplessly fits. Put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Helplessly means without being able to help yourself or do anything about a situation.
fact: Helplessly can also mean without being able to stop, as in «laughed helplessly».
fact: Helpless means having no power to help, and -ly turns it into an adverb that tells how something is done.
fact: In «cried freely and helplessly and openly», the word helplessly shows that Mole could not hold back his tears.
fact: Helplessly often shows that a character has no power in a moment, which makes readers feel sympathy or tension.
exercise: «Mole cried freely and helplessly and openly.» What does helplessly mean here? | Angrily and loudly | Happily, with a smile | Quietly, so no one could hear | *Without being able to stop
exercise: The children watched helplessly as the boat drifted out to sea. What does helplessly show? | They were fast asleep | They were bored and wanted to go home | They could cheer and celebrate | *They had no power to stop it
exercise: Find the word that helplessly is built from. | helpings | helper | *helpless | helpful
test: Jaya laughed helplessly at the silly joke. What does helplessly mean? | Rudely, to upset the others | *Unable to stop laughing | Politely and quietly | Sadly, with tears
test: Why is helplessly a useful word in stories? | It shows the story is about a holiday | It is a longer word than most | It shows that a character is very rich | *It shows a character has no power in that moment
exam: In «watches helplessly as something goes wrong», which word is the best swap for helplessly? | *Without power to change it | Cleverly | Happily | Quickly
